  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\r26041/001/A,\r26041/002/A,\r26041/003/A,\r26041/004/A,\r26041/005/A,\rAdult Gaming Centres Consumer Trends and Insights Report,\rMarketing Report (Murray Commercial Property Consultants),\rSecurity, Crime Prevention & Social Responsibility Statement,\rPremises Expansion Noise Assessment, \rPlanning Statement,\rWaste Management Plan.\rLondon Borough of Enfield Premises Licence.\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the details shown within the submitted drawings and documents, within three months of the date of this permission, details on a scheme of cycle parking shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \r\rA minimum of 1.no long stay cycle parking space shall be provided per 8 full-time staff.\rA minimum of 1.no short stay cycle parking space shall be provided for every 30 seats within the Adult Gaming Centre.\r\rThe proposed cycle parking shall fulfil the following:\r\rLocation: Near entrances or main access\rDesign: Stands or wall bars\rSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit \rCoverage: Covered Accessibility: \rStep-free, no obstructions\r\rThe approved cycle parking shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport. \r",
    "Notwithstanding the details shown within the submitted drawings and documents, within three months of the date of this permission, details on a scheme of waste and recycling storage for the site shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rThis shall indicate the exact siting of bins, the storage capacity of bins, and shall indicate the separate streams of waste to be provided. \r\rApproved refuse storage shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate waste and recycling storage facilities are provided to meet the needs of occupiers, promote sustainable waste management practices, and support borough-wide recycling targets. \r",
    "Within 3 months of the date of this permission, evidence of relevant Secured by Design certification shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: In the interest of creating safer, secure, sustainable communities.\r"
  ],
